f 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409684 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409684 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409684 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1a00ccd6-15ad-566e-9909-ced57101fb7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409685 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7a779adf-221a-5189-a14f-312c86e15c0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409686 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "98c176ba-da66-551c-9c0c-0c257e4d9459" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409687 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dc16361c-3306-5054-a003-e31388cab6e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=-7.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a80ad4c-5529-5931-9d7c-574d40c6f47e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409688 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $2,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $2$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $2$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =2\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-2det(B) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $Y$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(Y)=5.$ What is the value of $det(2Y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81c5993c-3d71-5869-bbf5-3e36b2df3a7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409689 #edb/ref 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2Y) & ={2}^{6}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1069 "q-43046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ac571f6-6f05-5f70-8bcf-34738f544556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409690 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72737" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(A)=-4.$ What is the value of $det(6A)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fded0a2c-cd1a-5de1-a671-20ea991daecd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409691 #edb/ref 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot A)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6A) & ={6}^{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0f93ad19-15c5-55b8-98ea-d5bcee8f0a3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409692 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2aef95ee-e7e9-5cac-b9ad-3b67a53db79f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2df25dd7-50b3-560b-9abe-b6b13654a237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409694 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e6fad07-ec42-5416-85eb-9ef2b0059cbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409695 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409696 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409696 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d75809ee-199d-50e2-b002-2326810f1174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175